The scheduler's tail calls vTaskSwitchContext before the task-exit error.

The kernel's own Cortex-M4F port ends xPortStartScheduler with a call to
vTaskSwitchContext and then prvTaskExitError, so that link-time optimisation
cannot drop either symbol; the SDK's nRF52 CMSIS port kept only the second.
The image has both, at 0x740b2 (vTaskSwitchContext@0x7333c) and inline
immediately after it: the ulDummy slot is written at 0x740b6 and the
load-compare spin is at 0x740c8.

--- a/CMSIS/nrf52/port_cmsis.c
+++ b/CMSIS/nrf52/port_cmsis.c
@@ -258,7 +258,9 @@
     /* Should never get here as the tasks will now be executing!  Call the task
     exit error function to prevent compiler warnings about a static function
     not being called in the case that the application writer overrides this
-    functionality by defining configTASK_RETURN_ADDRESS. */
+    functionality by defining configTASK_RETURN_ADDRESS. Call
+    vTaskSwitchContext() so link time optimisation does not remove the symbol. */
+    vTaskSwitchContext();
     prvTaskExitError();
 
     /* Should not get here! */
